Subject: [PATCH 2/2] docs(process): classify-effort - review fixes
 (placeholders, tie-break order, floor on the remainder)

- The label commands use quoted LEVEL/REASON placeholders and a heredoc,
  so nothing in them is read as a shell redirect or run as a command.
- The table row decides; the questions only break ties, in a stated order.
- The safety floor is restated for the remaining stage of an umbrella.
- Smaller notes from the review: needs-research wording, research-shaped
  work back in the max row, escalation kept apart from first
  classification, the sweep prints before applying and says what its
  query excludes; AGENTS.md says the skill never lowers a label.

